{* ctools-attribution:begin (generated by scripts/sync_attribution.py; edit config/attribution.json)}{...}
{marker acknowledgments}{...}
{title:Acknowledgments}

{pstd}
{cmd:cpsmatch} reimplements {cmd:psmatch2}, written by Edwin Leuven and
Barbara Sianesi. Its syntax, options, output, generated variables, and stored
results follow {cmd:psmatch2}.

{pstd}
{cmd:cpsmatch} is pinned to this version of {cmd:psmatch2}:

{p2colset 9 27 29 2}{...}
{p2col:Command}{cmd:psmatch2}{p_end}
{p2col:Authors}Edwin Leuven and Barbara Sianesi{p_end}
{p2col:Version}4.1.0{p_end}
{p2col:Date}June 11, 2026{p_end}
{p2col:Header line}{cmd:*! version 4.1.0 11jun2026 E. Leuven, B. Sianesi}{p_end}
{p2col:Source}SSC ({cmd:ssc install psmatch2}), distributed November 16,
2026.{p_end}
{p2col:Latest version?}Yes, as of November 25, 2026.{p_end}
{p2colreset}{...}

{pstd}
Until November 16, 2026, SSC distributed {cmd:psmatch2} 4.0.12 (January 30,
2016), and ctools 1.3.0 and earlier follow that version. Version 4.1.0 matches
the same observations and reports the same effects with different standard
errors. The default ATT standard error uses the outcome variance of every
control on support, {cmd:ate} has ATU and ATE standard errors without
{cmd:ai()}, and {cmd:ai()} reports the population variance unless
{cmd:samplevar} is specified and corrects for an estimated propensity score.
In 4.0.12, {cmd:ai()} reported the sample variance unless {cmd:population} was
specified. {cmd:which psmatch2} shows the version on your machine, and
{cmd:ssc install psmatch2, replace} installs 4.1.0.

{pstd}
{cmd:cpsmatch} changes only when ctools is updated to a newer version of
{cmd:psmatch2} and tested against it. {cmd:which psmatch2} shows the version
installed on your machine. {help ctools##acknowledgments:help ctools} lists
the pinned versions of all ctools commands.

{pstd}
Please report bugs and questions about {cmd:cpsmatch} at
{browse "https://github.com/mdroste/stata-ctools/issues":github.com/mdroste/stata-ctools/issues}.
The authors of {cmd:psmatch2} do not maintain {cmd:cpsmatch}. Undocumented
differences between {cmd:cpsmatch} and {cmd:psmatch2} are bugs in
{cmd:cpsmatch}.

{pstd}
If you use {cmd:cpsmatch} in published work, please cite the original command:

{phang2}Leuven, E., and B. Sianesi. 2003. PSMATCH2: Stata module to perform
full Mahalanobis and propensity score matching, common support graphing, and
covariate imbalance testing. Statistical Software Components S432001, Boston
College Department of Economics.{p_end}
{* ctools-attribution:end}{...}


